---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.ts';

const title = `Privacy — what ${SITE.name} keeps`;
const description = `What ${SITE.name} stores when you share a wish or light a star, and how that information is used.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }]} />
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short, because the site is short on excuses for collecting things.</p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose">
    <h2>What a submission stores</h2>
    <p>We store the project name, public homepage, category, description, uploaded product screenshot, optional maker wish, review state and relevant dates. Your email is used for receipt, review and essential service messages and is never shown on public pages. Submissions made while signed in are linked to your account so you can see progress and edit a pending submission.</p>
    <p>A one-way hash of the submitting IP address helps limit rapid repeated submissions. Rate limit records expire automatically.</p>

    <p>Screenshots are stored in Cloudflare R2. Pending and rejected screenshots are accessible only to the submitting account and authorized reviewers. After approval, the screenshot is published as the product cover. Withdrawing a pending submission deletes its screenshot. Do not upload screenshots that contain passwords, private messages or other confidential information.</p>

    <h2>What is published</h2>
    <p>
      Approved entries become a public page with the product name, its link, product description and screenshot, the dates we indexed and
      last checked it, and the blessing. Product descriptions may be supplied by an authorized submitter or an editor.
    </p>

    <h2>Community stars</h2>
    <p>The server issues an opaque HttpOnly browser cookie. We store its hash, expiry, project choices and vote dates for up to a year of browser identity validity. It is separate from your account and submission email. One star per project is recorded for that identity; it does not identify one natural person. Issuance and voting are rate limited.</p>
    <h2>Saved and followed projects</h2>
    <p>Saved projects and followed projects are associated with your account. Following a project enables essential email messages when its listing changes. You can stop following it from its project page. Correction requests and review decisions are kept with your account.</p>

    <h2>Tracking, cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      When a GA4 measurement ID is configured, Google Analytics runs by default to measure site visits and page activity.
      We do not send account fields, form contents or project prompts to Google Analytics. Analytics is configured with IP
      anonymization and advertising signals disabled; the site does not use advertising tags or cross-site ad tracking.
      Authentication uses a necessary, HttpOnly session cookie after you sign in.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Email accounts store your email address and a salted password hash. Email verification and password recovery links are single-use and expire
      after one day. Sign-in sessions are stored as one-way token hashes in D1 and use a necessary, HttpOnly, Secure cookie.
      Google sign-in stores the Google account identifier, verified email and display name needed to maintain your account.
      You can request account removal at <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>Submissions and their contact email are retained for review, service notifications and correction handling. Notification records track attempts, provider acceptance and errors; provider acceptance does not confirm inbox delivery. Expired sessions, email tokens, browser identities, rate limits and verification nonces are cleaned up automatically.</p>
    <p>You can withdraw a pending submission from your account. Contact <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a> to request removal of a published listing, account or retained contact information. These requests are handled by review.</p>

    <h2>Where it lives</h2>
    <p>
      Pages are served through Cloudflare. Submissions, accounts and sessions are stored in Cloudflare D1, and verification
      messages are sent through Cloudflare Email Service. Google sign-in uses a signed identity token that WishMeteor verifies;
      when GA4 is configured, page activity is sent to Google Analytics. Processing location and retention follow each provider's
      service settings and policies. The site is operated from the address on the <a href="/about">about page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
